# Signing and notarization credentials for macOS builds.
#
#   cp .env.example .env    then fill in the two blanks below.
#
# .env is gitignored and excluded from the packaged app. Nothing here is read
# at runtime; it exists for `npm run package:mac` and `npm run release`.

# ── Notarization ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# APPLE_APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD comes from appleid.apple.com > Sign-In and
# Security > App-Specific Passwords. Your Apple ID password is rejected.
APPLE_ID=
APPLE_APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD=
APPLE_TEAM_ID=

# An App Store Connect API key works instead of the three lines above, and is
# the better option if you already have one for TestFlight uploads:
# APPLE_API_KEY=/path/to/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8
# APPLE_API_KEY_ID=XXXXXXXXXX
# APPLE_API_ISSUER=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# ── Certificate ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave these empty for local builds: electron-builder finds the "Developer ID
# Application" identity in your login keychain on its own. They exist for CI,
# where the certificate has to travel as a base64-encoded .p12.
# CSC_LINK=
# CSC_KEY_PASSWORD=
